# LanCartographer .gitignore
#
# Two classes of generated/binary files are INTENTIONALLY CHECKED IN — do not
# "clean" them:
#
#   1. `*.syso` (currently cmd/lancartographer/resource.syso) — the Windows
#      version-resource object built by goversioninfo from versioninfo.json +
#      app.manifest + app.ico. It is embedded into every release build, so a
#      fresh clone must build without running `go generate` first.
#   2. internal/oui/oui_data.go — the embedded MAC-vendor (OUI) database,
#      generated from internal/oui/data.csv via `go generate ./internal/oui`.
#      Without it the vendor column compiles empty and the binary would need
#      a network fetch (which this project forbids: no phone-home).
#
# Both are regenerated only on demand; they are source for reproducible
# builds, not build output. The `!*.syso` negation below keeps the broad
# `*.exe`-style hygiene rules from swallowing them.

# Compiled binaries / build output
*.exe
!*.syso
dist/

# Test binaries and coverage
*.test
*.out
coverage*

# Vendored deps — this project does not vendor (module proxy + go.sum only)
/vendor/

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local scratch
.smoke/
.tmp-*
*.log

# Session scratch (superpowers SDD plans)
.superpowers/

# Fuzz corpora (regenerated by `go test -fuzz`)
testdata/fuzz/

# Go workspace files (this repo builds as a single module)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Profiling / trace artifacts (`go test -cpuprofile`, `-trace`, pprof output)
*.prof
*.pprof
*.trace
